<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
  <!--
    False positive: OWASP Dependency-Check matches the PyPI package `triton`
    (OpenAI Triton, a GPU kernel compiler pulled in transitively by torch on
    Linux) to CVE-2023-30859 via the CPE `cpe:2.3:a:triton_project:triton`.

    CVE-2023-30859 is unrelated to OpenAI Triton: it affects software with
    "bungee" enabled in its configuration, not a GPU compiler and not the
    NVIDIA Triton Inference Server. This service does not run the NVIDIA
    Triton Inference Server nor any bungee/Minecraft component; `triton` is
    present only as a transitive torch dependency on Linux and is never
    invoked as a network-facing server.

    pip-audit (advisory-database based) reports no vulnerabilities for this
    dependency set. This suppression is scoped to the single CVE on the
    triton package so every other finding continues to fail the build.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes><![CDATA[
      OpenAI Triton (PyPI, transitive dep of torch) mis-matched to
      CVE-2023-30859 (a bungee-config vulnerability). Name collision only.
    ]]></notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:pypi/triton@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2023-30859</cve>
  </suppress>
</suppressions>
